  "final_text": "**Kartovka (Brno, offer C) is cheapest, at about €24,910 a year, if paper prices stay flat.** Its paper surcharge can make it more expensive, though, so it's not a clear win.\n\nI compared the yearly cost for 40,000 boxes delivered to the plant. That includes the early-payment discount (you always take it), freight from your forwarder's contract, and external storage under your internal rules.\n\n| | A – Rednitz, Nürnberg | B – Wartapak, Poznań | C – Kartovka, Brno |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Boxes (40,000) | 0.66 € → 26,400 € | 0.52 € → 20,800 € | 0.575 € → 23,000 € |\n| After discount | −2 % → 25,872 € | −2 % → 20,384 € | −3 % → 22,310 € |\n| Cutting die (no discount) | 0 | 1,450 € | 0 |\n| Freight | 0 (delivered free to the plant) | 2 trips × 1,400 € = 2,800 € | 4 trips × 650 € = 2,600 € |\n| External storage | 0 (order in batches of 10,000 or less) | 20 pallets − 10 = 10 spaces × 16 € × 12 months = 1,920 € | 0 (each delivery is exactly 10 pallets) |\n| **Total per year** | **25,872 €** | **26,554 €** | **24,910 €** |\n\n**Things to know:**\n\n- **C's paper surcharge:** If the paper index rises between order and delivery, Kartovka charges 60 % of the €23,000 order value times the percentage rise, with no discount. That's €138 per percentage point. C stays cheaper than A only while the rise stays under **about 7 %** (€962 ÷ €138). Your orders are spread across all of 2027, so a 7 % rise is quite possible. Also, Kartovka hasn't said which index it uses yet.\n- **A is the safe choice:** €962 more per year (+3.9 %), but the price is fixed through the end of 2027. Delivery is five working days after you order, with a minimum of 3,000 boxes, so you have no freight or storage to manage.\n- **B is cheapest per box but most expensive overall.** The 20,000-box minimum order forces external storage, and freight and the die add more. Ordering all 40,000 at once would be worse still: you'd save €1,400 in freight but pay €5,760 for storage. The offer is also only valid until 30.11.2026 and doesn't say the price holds for 2027.\n- **Deadlines:** C's offer expires on **15.11.2026** (30 days from 16 October). Don't use A's 0.62 € price tier, because it only applies from 60,000 boxes a year.\n\n**My recommendation:** Before choosing C, ask Kartovka for a fixed price for 2027, or at least a cap on the surcharge and which index it uses. If they agree, C is the best choice. If not, I'd go with A, because its price can't rise.",
